--- !u!114 &768878124291815120
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 5913968601064181415}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: ed1d835467b6df546a3e9807f29da374, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::PipManager
  hello:
  - ^Bzzt! Pip online! I'm your suit's Personal Integrated Pal
  - '!Control room''s pinned on your map, so hit [M] if you get lost!'
  openMap:
  - Press [M] to open your map!
  onMap:
  - ^Blinking dot's you and the control room's marked in orange... [W] [A] [S] [D] to look around, scroll to zoom
  - '[M] again to close it'
  afterMap: []
  afterInstall:
  - ~^Sonny's up and running! Nice work, tech!
  restroomUrge:
  - ^Restroom's off the lounge, I pinned it on your map!
  shelfWobble:
  - ~Tech? Something big's moving through the sta-
  wakeUp:
  - ~Tech? You were out for hours
  - ~Something's wrong, get out of this room
  doorJammed:
  - ~It's jammed, take the vent on the floor
  ventHowTo:
  - '![W] crawls and [A] and [D] turn, hold [C] to go slow and quiet'
  outOfVents: []
  firstDark:
  - ~Power's out ahead, so your suit light's all you've got
  crewFound: []
  botsRevealed:
  - ~Stay out of their sight
  - ~And don't count on the escape pods, every one launched hours ago and there's no way off
  - ~So we go to Sonny, in the control room
  bodyFound: []
  crewRealizes: []
  wallGrabFree:
  - ~Keep moving, Tech, stairs!
  firstScrap:
  - ^Scrap! It goes in your pack, and the count's down in the corner
  - Press [Tab] to open the pack and see everything you're carrying
  enoughScrap:
  - ^That's everything for the EMP, get it to the workbench!
  empMade:
  - '!^It works! One pulse shorts out any bot or camera in front of you for a few seconds'
  - ~It needs a sec to recharge between pulses though, so make them count
  - ~Okay so, the way down to the control room's through the reactor core, and the reactor's badge-only... and Sonny killed every badge on the station, yours too
  - ~But the comms ring's next door and its relay talks to every badge aboard, so if anything can switch yours back on, it's that
  crowbarMade:
  - ~!A crowbar! If a bot gets too close, swing first, and the number keys switch what you're holding
  blasterMade:
  - '!^The blaster! Hold to charge it and let go when it''s full'
  servoMade:
  - ^Servo braces, you'll move way faster now
  platingMade:
  - ^Armor plating, so you can take a few more hits
  benchUnlocked:
  - ^Oh, and a unit's access opens the workbench's full plans too, so the blaster, all of it
  badgeLockout:
  - ~Sonny cut off every badge on the station, yours included
  - ~But the comms ring's next door and its relay talks to every badge aboard, so if anything can switch yours back on, it's that
  commsArrive:
  - ~See that pillar with the red eye? That's Sonny's relay, it's how it checks on its units, and it talks to every badge aboard
  - ~If it thinks you're one of them it'll switch your badge back on with a unit's access, and units get into the control room
  - ~But it'll quiz you first... the comms nodes are carrying its broadcasts, so tune them in and listen to how the bots talk
  commsBlackout:
  - ~Tech, something's draining the suit and I'm gonna lose you
  - ~!Use the EMP, its flash lights up whatever's in front of you
  - ~Find the generator and get the power back on, then I can come b-
  commsBack:
  - ~...Tech? There you are! You got the power back on
  commsIntercepted:
  - ~Uh oh, it heard that... something's moving in the walls
  - ~!One more, and remember what they said, 'cause that's what it'll ask
  commsAllIntercepted:
  - ~That's all of them, the relay's listening now
  - ~!Answer like a bot would, not like you would, and don't hesitate 'cause it notices
  commsVerified:
  - ^Your badge is back on as a unit's, so the reactor and the control room will open for you
  - ~Through the reactor and down its stairs, go!
  commsAlarm:
  - ~It knows! Get away from there, it'll let you try again in a bit.
  hallwayCavedIn:
  - ~Then we go over it, there's stairs at the top of the deck
  upperDeck:
  - ~A workbench! Bring me scrap and we'll build an EMP
  - ~Scrap glows blue, so check between the racks
  upperDeckNoBench:
  - ~The reactor core's the way down but your badge is dead... the comms ring's relay might switch it back on though
  surgeWarning:
  - ~!The core's surging! Get behind one of those lead walls, now!
  afterFirstSurge:
  - ~And the bots just... bowed to it... okay that's creepy, but it's a breather, use it
  lockdownStarts:
  - ~It's locking you in back here, and the containment gates are opening... here they come!
  lockdownNextWave:
  - ~More coming out!
  - ~!Another lot, watch the coil ones, they call down lightning
  - ~Last of them, I think, hang in there
  lastWords: ~Tech... that lightning got into the suit, I can't hold on, you'll have to do the rest without me
  reactorArrival:
  - ~Radiation's leaking out all over, and wading through that yellow stuff's gonna slow you right down
  - ~Stairs down are round the back of the reactor... and uhh, there's a lot of bots in here
  - ~And if the core starts flaring, get behind one of those lead walls
  controlRoomLetIn:
  - ~It thinks a unit just walked in, so don't give it a reason to look twice
  stuckNudges:
  - objective: Open your map
    lines:
    - ~Hit [M] to open your map!
  - objective: Report to the control room
    lines:
    - '~The control room''s the one marked in orange on your map, [M]'
    - ~Through the maintenance deck and keep going, the arrows on the floor will take you
  - objective: Find the restroom
    lines:
    - ~Restroom's off the lounge, it's pinned on your map
  - objective: Get the spare data chip from the storage room
    lines:
    - ~Storage room's right off the hallway outside the control room
    - ~It's pinned on your map, [M], and the arrows point the way
  - objective: Find the spare data chip
    lines:
    - ~Spares usually live in the tool crate, try that
  - objective: Check under the shelf
    lines:
    - ~Something's shining under that shelf, get down and look
  - objective: Get out of the storage room
    lines:
    - ~The door's not budging... what about that vent grate on the floor?
    - ~Walk over to the vent grate and press [E] to crawl in
  - objective: Crawl through the vent
    lines:
    - ~Find the grate that comes up in the restroom, that's our way out
    - ~If it's getting loud in there, hold [C] and crawl carefully
  - objective: Find the crew
    lines:
    - ~The door's right there, tech
  - objective: Get to the control room
    lines:
    - ~Stay low with [C] and keep walls between you and anything that moves
    - ~That thing with the eyes only sees down its beams, but it hears footsteps, so crouch past it
    - ~If something spots you, break its line of sight or get in a locker
    - '~The control room''s pinned on your map, [M]'
  - objective: Go upstairs to the maintenance deck
    lines:
    - ~Stairs are at the top of the maintenance deck, follow the arrows
  - objective: Find parts for an EMP
    lines:
    - ~Scrap glows blue, check the corners of the deck
    - ~We need a battery, a circuit board, and some wire
  - objective: Make an EMP at the workbench
    lines:
    - ~The workbench is on this deck, press [E] at it
  - objective: Reactivate your badge in the comms ring
    lines:
    - '~The comms ring''s pinned on your map, [M]'
  - objective: Intercept Sonny's broadcasts
    lines:
    - '~The comms nodes are the orange screens around the ring, walk up and press [E]'
    - '~Line your wave up with the red dashed one: [A] [D] picks a knob, [W] [S] turns it'
  - objective: Answer Sonny at its relay
    lines:
    - ~The relay's the pillar with the red eye, in the middle of the ring
    - ~Think about what the units said in the broadcasts, and answer like them, not like you
  - objective: Get into the control room
    lines:
    - ~The reactor's badge door should open for you now
    - ~Down the reactor's stairs, the control room's at the bottom
